        <body>
            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="0746" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg740"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 852.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction, numbered
                    970, of the 21st instant, which reached me this morning, with respect to the
                    rights of the United States in the harbor of Pago Pago, I have the honor to
                    acquaint you that I have just had an interview at the foreign office with the
                    Earl of Rosebery, to whom I communicated your views on the subject, by reading
                    to his lordship your instruction, of which I left a copy with him at his
                    request.</p>
                <p>Lord Rosebery promised to give the matter his prompt attention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
